  "_comment": [
    "Alias resolution is exact-string, applied to an already normalized value (trimmed,",
    "lowercased, whitespace collapsed, surrounding punctuation stripped). Keys are normalized",
    "aliases, values are the canonical form that both the model output and the gold value are",
    "resolved to before comparison. It is never substring replacement and aliases never chain.",
    "",
    "A leading article is already dropped by the normalizer before this table is consulted, so",
    "'the platform team' and 'platform team' need no entry here. The table exists for the rest:",
    "a surname resolves to the full name it belongs to, and a handful of phrases the corpus",
    "writes one way and a model would write another are mapped. There is deliberately no alias",
    "for the bare first name Ravi or the bare first name Anna: two people carry each of those in",
    "this corpus, so only the full names and the surnames resolve, and a reply that says only",
    "'Ravi' is not an answer."
